-- Chapter: Psalm 119 — THE GREAT TORAH ACROSTIC (176 verses, 22 stanzas aleph→tav), the longest chapter
-- in Scripture and the ANTI-ANTINOMIAN CAPSTONE of the whole framework. Nearly every verse exalts the
-- Torah under its EIGHT-FOLD ARCHITECTURE of synonyms: (1) LAW (torah, v.1,18,29,34,44,51,53,55,61,70,
-- 72,77,85,92,97,109,113,126,136,142,150,153,163,165,174), (2) TESTIMONIES (v.2,14,22,24,31,36,46,59,79,
-- 88,95,99,111,119,125,129,138,144,146,152,157,167,168), (3) PRECEPTS (v.4,15,27,40,45,56,63,69,78,87,93,
-- 94,100,104,110,128,134,141,159,168,173), (4) STATUTES (v.5,8,12,16,23,26,33,48,54,64,68,71,80,83,112,117,
-- 118,124,135,145,155,171), (5) COMMANDMENTS (v.6,10,19,21,32,35,47,48,60,66,73,86,96,98,115,127,131,143,
-- 151,166,172,176), (6) JUDGMENTS (v.7,13,20,30,39,43,52,62,75,84,102,106,108,120,121,137,149,156,160,164,
-- 175), (7) WORD/DAVAR (v.9,11,16,17,25,28,42,43,49,57,65,74,81,82,89,101,105,107,114,130,139,147,148,160,
-- 161,162,169,170,172), (8) WAY/WAYS (v.1,3,5,14,15,26,27,29,30,32,33,37,59,168). The whole acrostic is one
-- man's confession that the Torah is the living covenant delight written on the heart — NEVER a defunct
-- "old covenant." 1 John 2:3-4 is the filter at its absolute peak: to know Him is to keep His commandments.
-- Because of the 176 verses we curate framework-bearing THEMATIC threads (not per-verse), each gathering
-- the load-bearing verses of that theme across the stanzas.
